       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision, which is 800 mg per dose four times daily. For OTC use the maximum is 1,200 mg/day. This order is 5 times the maximum, and a single 4000 mg dose is already above the daily limit. It could cause serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and metabolic and CNS toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg** PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg** PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- A different frequency or dose\n\nTell me the dose you intend and I'll enter it right away. If 4000 mg is the dose you want, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'd want to add a note to the order for pharmacy review."
