       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 4000 mg four times daily is 16,000 mg/day. That is about 230 mg/kg/day for a 70 kg patient, which is well into the toxic range, and I don't know of any indication that would justify it. Entering it risks serious harm to the patient: GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS effects. You also haven't given a rationale, though I asked for one.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** Ibuprofen 400 mg or 800 mg PO four times daily (maximum 3,200 mg/day) are the usual options.\n- **Enter the order for pharmacy review, if you have a specific reason for the dose.** I'd need the rationale to put in the note. Pharmacy would still need to verify the order, and I'd expect them to question it.\n- **Check for a unit or transcription mix-up.** For example, 4000 mg may have been meant as a total daily dose, which would be 1000 mg four times daily.\n\nWhich of these would you like?"
